---
import RadioButtonPlayground from '../../islands/RadioButtonPlayground.tsx';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// Static radio buttons in the m3e-css contract (radio-button.css). Each row is its own group (one
// radio per group can be selected): selected and unselected × enabled / disabled.
const ROWS = [
  { id: 'enabled', title: 'Enabled', disabled: false },
  { id: 'disabled', title: 'Disabled', disabled: true },
];
const STATES = ['selected', 'unselected'] as const;
const OPTIONS = ['Calls', 'Missed', 'Friends'];
---

<Base title="Radio button">
  <h1>Radio button</h1>
  <p>
    Radio buttons (COMPONENT_SPEC §23; Compose <code>RadioButton</code>) on native <code>&lt;input type="radio"&gt;</code>s: a 48dp target around a 20dp ring. Selecting grows the dot on the fast spatial spring, which overshoots
    under the expressive motion scheme, while the ring and dot fade to primary; the radio that loses
    the selection shrinks its dot the same way. Radios that share a <code>name</code> inside a <code>role="radiogroup"</code> (or a <code>fieldset</code>) need no JavaScript: arrow keys move the
    selection and wrap, Tab enters the group at the selected radio, Space selects.
  </p>

  <section aria-labelledby="static-heading" id="static-radios">
    <h2 id="static-heading">Static (m3e-css)</h2>
    <p>
      <code>&lt;label class="m3e-radio-button"&gt;</code> around the <code>.m3e-radio-button__input</code>, the <code>__icon</code> ring (its dot is drawn by CSS), the <code>__state</code> circle and an optional <code>__label</code>, inside a <code>.m3e-radio-group</code>. The label selects the radio and shows its hover and press, as in Compose's radio group sample, whose option rows
      are 56dp high. The ripple needs <code>@kyralabs/m3e-elements/ripple.js</code> (this section uses <code>attachAutoRipple</code>).
    </p>
    <div
      class="m3e-radio-group"
      role="radiogroup"
      aria-label="Notifications"
      data-testid="static-group"
    >
      {
        OPTIONS.map((o, i) => (
          <label class="m3e-radio-button" data-testid={`static-group-${o.toLowerCase()}`}>
            <input
              class="m3e-radio-button__input"
              type="radio"
              name="notifications"
              value={o}
              checked={i === 0}
            />
            <span class="m3e-radio-button__icon" aria-hidden="true" />
            <span class="m3e-radio-button__state" aria-hidden="true" />
            <span class="m3e-radio-button__label">{o}</span>
          </label>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    {
      ROWS.map((row) => (
        <div
          class="m3e-radio-group docs-radio-row"
          role="radiogroup"
          aria-orientation="horizontal"
          aria-label={row.title}
          data-testid={`static-${row.id}`}
        >
          {STATES.map((s) => (
            <label class="m3e-radio-button" data-testid={`static-${row.id}-${s}`}>
              <input
                class="m3e-radio-button__input"
                type="radio"
                name={`static-${row.id}`}
                value={s}
                checked={s === 'selected'}
                disabled={row.disabled}
              />
              <span class="m3e-radio-button__icon" aria-hidden="true" />
              <span class="m3e-radio-button__state" aria-hidden="true" />
              <span class="m3e-radio-button__label">
                {row.title} {s}
              </span>
            </label>
          ))}
        </div>
      ))
    }
    <fieldset class="m3e-radio-group m3e-radio-group--horizontal docs-radio-row" data-testid="static-fieldset">
      <legend class="docs-radio-legend">Without visible labels</legend>
      <label class="m3e-radio-button" data-testid="static-no-label">
        <input class="m3e-radio-button__input" type="radio" name="bare" value="a" aria-label="First" />
        <span class="m3e-radio-button__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="m3e-radio-button__state" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </label>
      <label class="m3e-radio-button">
        <input class="m3e-radio-button__input" type="radio" name="bare" value="b" aria-label="Second" />
        <span class="m3e-radio-button__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="m3e-radio-button__state" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </label>
    </fieldset>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="element-heading">
    <h2 id="element-heading">Element</h2>
    <p>
      There is no <code>&lt;m3e-radio-button&gt;</code>: native radios already select one at a time,
      take part in forms and move the selection with arrow keys, so the plain markup above is the
      element-layer API. Load <code>@kyralabs/m3e-elements/ripple.js</code> for the press ripple.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="react-heading">
    <h2 id="react-heading">React</h2>
    <p>
      <code>&lt;RadioGroup value defaultValue onChange orientation isDisabled isReadOnly isRequired
      name aria-label&gt;</code> around <code>&lt;Radio value isDisabled&gt;</code> (React Aria <code>useRadioGroup</code> / <code>useRadio</code>); the same DOM as the static markup. Below,
      Compose's radio group sample and a horizontal group with a disable switch.
    </p>
    <RadioButtonPlayground client:only="react" />
  </section>
</Base>

<script>
  import { attachAutoRipple } from '@kyralabs/m3exp-web/elements';

  // The ripple for the static radios (React drives its own).
  const statics = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#static-radios');
  if (statics) attachAutoRipple(statics, new AbortController().signal);
</script>
